      "problem": "$-{z}^{3}(4{z}^{2}-2z)=$",
      "worked_solution": "We multiply each term inside the parentheses by the term outside the parentheses, simplify using the rules of exponents, and then we add the results together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{z}^{3}(4{z}^{2}-2z) & = \\\\ (-{z}^{3})(4{z}^{2})+(-{z}^{3})(-2z) & = \\\\ ((-1)\\cdot 4)({z}^{3}\\cdot {z}^{2})+((-1)\\cdot (-2))({z}^{3}\\cdot z) & = \\\\ (-4){z}^{3+2}+(2){z}^{3+1} & = \\\\ -4{z}^{5}+2{z}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
